cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Grain-Growth Chunking: Structure-Aware Document Chunking for Retrieval"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Choudhary
    given-names: Mudit
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-8880-0925"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mudit-choudhary/grain-growth-chunking"
url: "https://github.com/mudit-choudhary/grain-growth-chunking"
abstract: >-
  A chunk grows by accepting the next block whole and keeps growing until it
  reaches a size budget or meets a structural barrier — a section heading, or a
  block that must stand alone such as a table. Barriers are absolute, so a chunk
  never crosses one. Evaluated against fixed-token and recursive character
  splitters in a pre-registered comparison over a 514-paper corpus.
keywords:
  - chunking
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - information retrieval
  - document structure
